{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785702206,"nonce":"ck7z2cRYg5WUGhqcOVPmbuXLAUI=","message":"**Design DECIDED 2026-08-03 (grill session; ADR-0066), and one finding INVERTS this ticket's premise.**\n\nThis ticket said HA reads need nothing and writes need \"fence affinity, not sharding\" — treating affinity as a routing convenience. **It is a correctness requirement the moment N\u003e1, and not only in the failure case.** `CONCURRENCY = 16` (`workspace-client/src/lib.rs:64`) means the drain opens up to 16 connections and kube-proxy load-balances PER CONNECTION, so a single fence's blobs scatter across replicas; `post_drain`'s closure validation then runs against ONE replica's ledger and warm tier and fails. That is every drain, every time, as soon as you scale past one — not a rare failure mode. The validation cannot be relaxed: the ledger check IS the cross-fence exfiltration fix from `e58ce1f`.\n\n**Mechanism:** affinity by RECORDED CHOICE, hashed by **Run** (not fence) so every step of a Run lands on one replica and step 2 finds step 1's content warm. The control plane picks at launch, stamps the address into the Pod env (where `WorkspaceFetch.url` already goes), and **reads it back off the Pod spec** for the drain GET and the flush — the Pod spec is already the durable record that survives a CP restart, same pattern as `ANNOTATION_WS_OUTPUTS`. No new column, no hash ring, no migration.\n\n**Costs:** the Service must become headless for per-pod DNS, and `service-workspace.yaml`'s comment (\"Deliberately NOT headless… nothing addresses an individual workspace replica\") MUST change with the code or the next reader will undo this. `WorkspaceFetch.url` stops being one field stamped identically into every Pod. Inert at N=1.\n\n**Also decided:** the drain record stays replica-local and its ABSENCE becomes transient rather than `FatalConfig` (see the sequencing note on `e140121`), which removes the one piece of non-rebuildable replica-local state without moving it to shared storage.\n\n**Sequencing: `e140121` MUST land first.** HA is meaningless while a replica reschedule dead-letters the runs in flight.","files":null}]}